{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesYwmRBFXpQEPwf7wxur","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have a clear understanding of the repository structure. Now let me move to the design phase.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add new error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the ErrorCode enum to handle attempts to confirm a shipment in an invalid state (CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint that:\n   - Takes the shipmentId as a path variable\n   - Retrieves the shipment; if not found, throws ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns success without changes (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n   - Returns the updated (or unchanged) shipment with 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four new tests:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and returns unchanged shipment\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\nI considered reusing an existing error code like `VALIDATION_FAILED` or creating no error code and just using 409 without a specific code. However, this violates the established convention that each meaningful error state has its own ErrorCode enum value, which allows clients to branch on stable codes. Adding `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` is the right approach.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):*\n- Client: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n- Controller: Retrieve shipment from repository\n- Logic: Check status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save to repository\n- Response: 200 OK, return updated Shipment\n\n*Idempotent path (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED):*\n- Client: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n- Controller: Retrieve shipment from repository\n- Logic: Check status is already CONFIRMED, return unchanged\n- Response: 200 OK, return same Shipment\n\n*Error path (CANCELLED):*\n- Client: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm`\n- Controller: Retrieve shipment from repository\n- Logic: Check status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException\n- Handler: GlobalExceptionHandler catches and returns 409 with error envelope\n- Response: 409 CONFLICT, body: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": []}}`\n\n*Error path (not found):*\n- Client: `POST /shipments/missing/confirm`\n- Controller: findById returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException\n- Handler: GlobalExceptionHandler catches and returns 404 with error envelope\n- Response: 404 NOT FOUND, body: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": []}}`\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: confirm CREATED shipment** - Create S-1 in CREATED, POST confirm, verify status becomes CONFIRMED, assert 200 OK and status field\n2. **Test: confirm CONFIRMED shipment (idempotent)** - Create S-2, confirm once, confirm again, verify status stays CONFIRMED, assert 200 OK\n3. **Test: confirm CANCELLED shipment** - Directly insert CANCELLED shipment, POST confirm, assert 409 CONFLICT with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED code\n4. **Test: confirm non-existent shipment** - POST confirm for S-missing, assert 404 NOT FOUND with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1074,"cache_read_input_tokens":17377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1074},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6173d706-0e62-4923-a9cb-5ed0c0f309e8","uuid":"4bcd190d-5251-4ef6-86d5-e36462691f53","timestamp":"2026-09-09T08:29:48.999Z","request_id":"req_011CesYwkZ5Gxy7NU3GnK5eX"}
