{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesYztmn2nEs8R5gZZedK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass, including the 4 new tests I added. The output shows:\n- **Tests run: 17, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0**\n- **BUILD SUCCESS**\n- ShipmentControllerTest: 9 tests (5 existing + 4 new confirm tests)\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** - `./mvnw test` completed successfully with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** - All 5 existing ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass (creating, reading, listing, duplicate rejection, not found handling)\n3. ✅ **`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it** - Test `confirms a created shipment and moves it to confirmed status` verifies this; status changes from CREATED to CONFIRMED\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with rest of API** - Uses existing ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException, integrated with GlobalExceptionHandler, follows error envelope pattern\n5. ✅ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** - Three separate tests cover all cases:\n   - `confirming an already confirmed shipment succeeds and changes nothing` - idempotent behavior\n   - `confirming a cancelled shipment returns 409 with error code` - SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n   - `confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error code` - SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** - Only added code to existing modules, no changes to pom.xml\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only modified:\n   - ApiError.kt (added ErrorCode enum value)\n   - ShipmentController.kt (added confirm endpoint)\n   - ShipmentControllerTest.kt (added tests)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Added `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to ErrorCode enum. This was necessary because a new error condition exists (attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment). This follows the established pattern where each meaningful error state has its own code.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added `confirm` method with:\n   - @PostMapping decorator for the confirm endpoint\n   - Path variable for shipmentId\n   - Proper error handling: ResourceNotFoundException for missing shipments, ConflictException for CANCELLED shipments\n   - Idempotent logic: CONFIRMED shipments return unchanged\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.ok() with updated/unchanged shipment\n   - This follows the exact same pattern as the existing create endpoint\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 4 tests:\n   - Test for normal CREATED→CONFIRMED transition\n   - Test for idempotent CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED behavior\n   - Test for CANCELLED rejection with 409 and error code\n   - Test for missing shipment with 404 and error code\n   - All tests follow existing patterns with MockMvc assertions on both status and response body\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are satisfied.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint that transitions CREATED shipments to CONFIRMED with idempotent, error-safe behavior for invalid states and missing resources\nChanged       ApiError.kt (added SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED ErrorCode enum value)\nChanged       ShipmentController.kt (added confirm endpoint with state transition logic)\nChanged       ShipmentControllerTest.kt (added 4 tests for confirm: normal transition, idempotency, cancelled rejection, not found handling)\nTests         1: confirms CREATED→CONFIRMED; 2: confirms CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED (idempotent); 3: confirms CANCELLED returns 409; 4: confirms missing returns 404\nVerification  ./mvnw test from sample-service/ → BUILD SUCCESS, 17 tests run, 0 failures\nNot done      None\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_inpu